// CTL-L2 — a request or response DTO is a projection of a canonical schema,
// built with `.pick`/`.omit`/`.extend`. Written by hand it stops being a
// projection: the canonical schema tightens a field and the transport keeps
// accepting the old one.
$node where {
  $node <: or {
    r"type\s+\w*(?:Request|Response|Dto|DTO)\s*=\s*\{[\s\S]*\}",
    r"interface\s+\w*(?:Request|Response|Dto|DTO)\s*\{[\s\S]*\}"
  },
  register_diagnostic(
    span = $node,
    message = "CTL-L2: derive the DTO from the canonical schema (`.pick`/`.extend`) and infer its type — a hand-written DTO drifts from the contract."
  )
}
